# What's New Copy Style

When adding a new `FeatureRelease` entry to `feature-releases.ts`, follow these rules:

## Voice & tone
- Write for the user, not the developer. Describe what they can **do** or **see**, not how it works internally.
- Present tense, active voice: "Track sessions…", "Edit habits…", "The header shows…"
- No technical jargon: no "DB-level", "ISO timestamps", "schema cache", "effective day boundary", etc.

## Bullets
- One sentence each. Lead with the action or benefit.
- ✅ "Track sessions that run past midnight — they show up on both days automatically."
- ❌ "Sessions that cross the configured day-reset boundary are now stored as a single ActivityPeriod and rendered via UI-level clipping."

## Fixes
- Plain statement of what was broken and now works.
- ✅ "Habit timers now show only the time tracked today, not the full session."
- ❌ "getActivityElapsedMs now clips via clipPeriodToDay instead of using raw start–end diff."

## Title
- Short noun phrase describing the theme, not a changelog tag.
- ✅ "Overnight sessions & smarter timeline"
- ❌ "fix: split-period-at-reset refactor + 7-day editable window"
